# The build context only needs preset/ and config/ -- the paths the
# Dockerfile COPYs. Everything else is dead weight, and some of it is heavy:
# .git also carries the unreachable blobs of `docker save` tarballs staged
# before .gitignore existed, and tmp/ holds the tarball on its way to
# `sbx template load`.
#
# Written as an allowlist -- "*" followed by ! exceptions, which is Docker's
# documented way to say what to include rather than what to exclude. It fails
# closed: COPYing some new path means allowing it here deliberately, instead
# of the rest of the repo riding along unnoticed.
#
# This does not change what today's build ships. BuildKit already narrows the
# filesync to the paths a COPY names, so the context transfer was already only
# a few hundred bytes. It is a guard for the day the Dockerfile grows a
# broader COPY, or something builds with DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 and the legacy
# builder sends the whole directory.
*
!preset
!config
